    "reviewer": "claude-code agent (S308) — rendered-pixel review of the theme matrix plus focused component captures of the new dispatch CTA",
    "findings": [
      "The 1366x900 theme-matrix captures are viewport-clipped, so the newly added Dispatch CTA sits below the fold and never appears in them. A green matrix alone would have proved nothing about the surface this session changed, so the CTA element was captured directly (.cache/cta-shots) in dark, light, high-contrast and lava at desktop, plus dark and light at 390px.",
      "BLOCKING DEFECT FOUND AND FIXED — light theme: the Subscribe button used a flat background:var(--gold) with near-black ink. In light theme --gold is #7a5c00, a dark amber the design system intends as TEXT on cream, so dark-on-dark fell under WCAG AA. Only visible in rendered pixels; source review looked correct.",
      "Fix reuses the sitewide .button treatment instead of re-deciding the palette locally: its gradient keeps bright stops at both edges in every theme, so button contrast is the design systems decision made once. Re-captured and confirmed legible in light, dark, high-contrast and lava.",
      "Mobile at 390px: the CTA collapses to a single column, the input is 16px (no iOS focus-zoom) and the button goes full width. No clipping, overlap or horizontal scroll.",
      "Hub headline now reads Six minds. One record. from the derived roster count, and the editorial-board grid reflows 3-up to 2-up to 1-up without orphaned cards."
    ],
    "fixesApplied": [
      "Replaced the CTA buttons flat gold background with the sitewide .button class (light-theme WCAG AA failure).",
      "Added a 761-1080px breakpoint so the six-persona board reflows two-up instead of squeezing three."
    ],
    "blockingDefectsOpen": 0
  },
